WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.196
Before writing an aggregation query use this
five-step workflow First

00:00:06.407 --> 00:00:10.357
ask the decision question What are we trying to
learn from the

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:16.030
data Second set the grain Decide what one

00:00:16.056 --> 00:00:22.056
output row should represent One diagnosis One
category

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:28.646
One department Third choose the measures That

00:00:28.672 --> 00:00:32.014
might be a count a total an average a minimum or a

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:37.928
maximum Fourth decide which rows qualify and which
groups qualify

00:00:38.865 --> 00:00:44.492
This is where WHERE and HAVING play different roles
Finally validate the

00:00:44.518 --> 00:00:50.060
summary against the detail data The most important
step is grain

00:00:50.997 --> 00:00:54.260
If you cannot describe one result row in a short
sentence do

00:00:54.273 --> 00:00:59.049
not rush into GROUP BY yet Clarify the intended
summary first
